AT LATER TIPS — how to apply it after the base has moved
  At `af12049` and every descendant, EXACTLY ONE of the 18 files fails:
    session_2026-07-30/item279_step4/scripts/harness_pvc_REPINNED.py
  It fails because it DUPLICATES a change that `af12049` already committed — the harness
  re-pin EXPECT_V0SURF '12d903336f6e' -> '96d671c952c8'. It is not a conflict of substance.

  git apply --binary \
    --exclude='session_2026-07-30/item279_step4/scripts/harness_pvc_REPINNED.py' \
    L3_T1_state.diff
  -> 17 files · data/v0surf.pkl = 84fb0cde29f36c1a91d440e63b753c3c · fv 95277b76
     IDENTICAL RESULT. Re-run at `abf8f4c` by this seat.
  Or regenerate the diff at the tip; both routes were measured to the same bytes.

THE CARRIER-COMMIT CLAUSE — why the base cannot be named as a main commit
  17 of the 18 targets are byte-identical at `79ee8e5` and at `origin/main`.
  The 18th — `harness_pvc_REPINNED.py` — DOES NOT EXIST ON MAIN at all: the step-4
  evidence pack lives only on the #290 line. So "this diff applies at main" is false for
  the one file that decides the question, and a base named as a main commit would be a
  true statement about 17 files and a wrong one about the diff.
  **A state diff's base names a commit on the line that carries all of its targets.**

THE INSTRUMENT, AND ITS LIMIT — stated so this annotation is not over-read
  `state_diff_base_probe.py` (beside this tree) tests a candidate base from the diff's own
  `index <pre>..<post>` lines, without applying anything. Run captured at
  `BASE_PROBE_L3_T1.txt`. Result:

      ADMISSIBLE SET: 6 commits — 3d253c6 … 79ee8e5, newest 79ee8e5

  The probe returns an INTERVAL, not a point: any commit that did not touch the diff's
  targets is indistinguishable from any other. `79ee8e5` is the NEWEST admissible commit
  and the one the generating act names. **Measurement narrows; provenance decides.**
  That is precisely why the base must be recorded when the diff is cut — and why this
  file exists rather than a recipe for recovering it later.

NON-VACUITY — the probe rejects, on both available grounds, in the captured run
  pre-image MISMATCH  abf8f4c · 6128b20 · af12049   (harness blob differs)
  target ABSENT       e73e6bf · 987a508 · 6081f8e   (harness not on main's line)
